{
    "toolName": "practice_questions_quiz_tool",
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "designSystem": "Singularity",
    "description": "An interactive multiple-choice quiz tool for Grade 7 Science (NCERT Chapter 3, Practice Questions). Redesigned with Singularity design system — Poppins font, #4A4DC9 primary indigo, #FF7212 highlight orange, #533086→#FC9145 warm gradient, pill-shaped buttons (40px radius) with proper Enabled/Hover/Pressed/Disabled states, #C1C1EA/#FFF3E4 light tints, clean card UI. Seven questions testing key chapter concepts: (Q1) classifying electricity uses — ceiling fan is cooling not transportation. (Q2) conductor vs insulator in a circuit — rubber eraser blocks current. (Q3) series circuit behaviour — if one lamp breaks, the other stops too. (Q4) cell symbol terminals — longer line is positive. (Q5) switch function — completes or breaks the circuit. (Q6) LED polarity — wrong polarity is most common reason for no glow. (Q7) troubleshooting — dead cell, fused lamp, loose wire are valid faults.",
    "designTokens": {
        "colors": {
            "primary": "#4A4DC9",
            "primaryDark": "#3A3DB0",
            "primaryDeep": "#533086",
            "highlight": "#FF7212",
            "highlightDark": "#E5660F",
            "gradientOrange": "#FC9145",
            "lightPurple": "#C1C1EA",
            "lightOrange": "#FFF3E4",
            "neutralDark": "#4E4E4E",
            "neutralMuted": "#8A8A8A",
            "gray300": "#CACACA",
            "gray200": "#EBEBEB",
            "gray100": "#F5F5F5",
            "white": "#FFFFFF"
        },
        "gradients": {
            "warm": "linear-gradient(135deg, #533086 0%, #FC9145 100%)",
            "primary": "linear-gradient(135deg, #533086 0%, #4A4DC9 40%, #FC9145 100%)",
            "subtle": "linear-gradient(135deg, #C1C1EA 0%, #FFF3E4 100%)"
        },
        "typography": {
            "fontFamily": "Poppins",
            "weights": [
                400,
                500,
                600,
                700,
                800,
                900
            ]
        },
        "borderRadius": {
